# Line-ending policy.
#
# Why this file exists: on 2026-07-28 this repo was cloned onto a Windows host
# for the first time and 83 of 87 tracked files checked out CRLF, because there
# was no policy here and Git for Windows defaults to `core.autocrlf=true`. The
# content was identical -- but that is exactly the failure mode that cost the
# sibling DJI-ATAK project a debugging session (its ERRATA E-005: 104 files
# converted LF -> CRLF with ZERO content changes). This project is now edited
# from both Windows and Linux, so without an explicit policy it recurs.
#
# Rule: everything textual is LF in the repo AND in the working tree.

* text=auto eol=lf

# Sources and docs -- explicit so intent survives a future `text=auto` change.
*.py            text eol=lf
*.md            text eol=lf
*.toml          text eol=lf
*.cfg           text eol=lf
*.ini           text eol=lf
*.txt           text eol=lf
*.yml           text eol=lf
*.yaml          text eol=lf
LICENSE         text eol=lf

# If a Windows batch entry point is ever added it must be CRLF, or cmd.exe
# mis-parses it. Listed pre-emptively so the rule is never rediscovered.
*.bat           text eol=crlf
*.cmd           text eol=crlf

# Binary assets -- never touch these, never try to diff them as text.
# .npy/.npz matter here: T-1.0 established a shared binary fixture, and a
# newline "fix" applied to a numpy array is silent, total corruption.
*.docx          binary
*.npy           binary
*.npz           binary
*.png           binary
*.jpg           binary
*.jpeg          binary
*.pdf           binary
